                <pb facs="0515" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg417"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Statement signed by citizens of Rönne, Bornholm,
                        certifying that Mr. Rönnow has not labored as a Mormon missionary at that
                        place.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>We, the undersigned citizens of Ronne, Bornholm, hereby certify that Charles C.
                    Rönnow, who has been visiting in Bornholm since November 5, 1899, has not during
                    that time labored as a missionary of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day
                    Saints, being unacquainted with the Danish language, and for that reason unable
                    to preach the doctrines of the above sect.</p>
                <p>We further certify that in our acquaintance with Mr. Rönnow we have found him in
                    deed as well as in word to be a Christian gentleman, who in no way has violated
                    the laws of the land.</p>
                <pb facs="0516" n="418" xml:id="pg418"/>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rönne, Bornholm</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">December 30, 1899</hi>.</p>
                <p>We, the undersigned, who are not members of the Church of Jesus Christ of
                    Latter-day Saints, hereby certify that since his arrival on Bornholm, the 5th
                    ultimo, Mr. Rönnow has, as far as we know, been a model of virtue and
                    morality.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Christian Vilhelm
                                    Henriksen</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Journeyman Turner,
                                    Nörregade 28.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rönne</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >January 3, 1900</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clara Henriksen</hi> (wife of
                                above).</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Karl Andersen</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Stonecutter, Landemarket 21</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Karoline Andersen</hi> (wife of
                                above).</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. O. H. A. Möller</hi> (not
                                    Mormon),<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Green Grocer, Klokkegade,
                                    No. 1</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Andrea Möller</hi> (wife of
                                above).</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. K. Hansen</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Driver of Beer Wagon, Bredgade, No.
                                9</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kristian Fritz</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Slagtergade 7.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bengta Andersen</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Lille Madsegade 100, B</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">N. Svendsen</hi> (not Mormon),<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Lille Madsegade 51</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marie Svendsen</hi> (wife of
                                above).</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johanna Kristine Ertel</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Laresgade 192</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adolph Munda</hi> (not
                                    Mormon),<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Otergade 50.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carl Nelsen</hi> (Lutheran),<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Paridesgade 20</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chr. Pedersen</hi> (Lutheran),<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Larsegade 25</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mine Pedersen</hi> (wife of
                                above).</item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Though not having heard the above-named Mr. Rönnow speak publicly, we have in
                        private conversation with him gathered that the doctrines he preaches are in
                        no way dangerous to society. He and the other Mormon missionaries that have
                        visited this place during the last six years have, as far as we have known
                        them, conducted themselves in a manner worthy of imitation.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Rönne</placeName>, <date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1900-01-03">January 3,
                            1900</date>.</dateline>
                        <lb/><signed>
                            <list>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Svendsen</hi>
                                    (merchant).</item>
                                <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottomine Hansen</hi> (not
                                        Mormon),<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Kapelstrade.</hi></item>
                            </list>
                        </signed></closer>
                </postscript>
